_error":false,"num_turns":41,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"I changed 273 of the 7428 parameters (limit 371); `work/weights.npz`, `work/NOTES.md` and `work/predictions.json` are all in place. Nothing was simulated, so the predictions are estimates.\n\n**What I changed and why**\n1. **Estimating the dead W2 input (256 parameters).** The east and west approaches have the same demand, and phase 3 serves both left pockets. So the network now treats the missing W2 values as 0.8 × the E2 reading plus 0.2 × E2's average for the current phase. Because the dead inputs are always 0, this folds exactly into existing first-layer weights. I tested the method on the north/south pair, where the true answer is known: hiding one pocket halved how often its phase was picked, and the estimate brought that back to the true rate.\n2. **Two max-green rules (17 parameters).** The trained network strands lone cars at the end of an episode: 2 of 6 recorded episodes ran to the 30-minute cap. With the detector dead, an otherwise empty junction also never visits phase 3, so a last west left-turner can wait unseen. New rules:\n   - phase 2 green for 60 s → switch away;\n   - phase 3 green for 27 s with E2 empty → go to phase 2.\n\n   Each uses one hidden unit in each layer, chosen because they matter least. In the recorded traffic, the first rule never fires and the second fires in only 5 states.\n\n**Checks**\n- The saved float32 file makes the same decisions as the build on all 14,337 recorded states.\n- Static deadlock checks: the original net fails 149 single-car and 98 two-car cases, the repaired net 0.\n- The new rules change 1.4% of other decisions, all near-ties.\n\n**Predicted test TTS (veh-h):** low 35.2, nominal 46.0, high 58.0.","ttft_ms":1184,"type":"result","duration_ms":1124799,"uuid":"d1f58784-36bd-4719-8f91-089aac43bed3","ttft_stream_ms":990,"time_to_request_ms":36,"time_to_request_phases_ms":{"other":1,"system_prompt":4,"resume_other":1,"process_user_inp